# K03 NS-ROLES-2 (Codex K03-NS-ROLES-2-20261007-20; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption,
# #declaration-visibility): a named Structure's body takes the common roles of the root and a method.
# Implementation limit (not a rule): `b: tick` in Host's body, tick a method -- the binding to the callable
# occurrence that the root and a method build -- is not held by a named body yet.  Said at tick.
fn: tick (int: n) int
    return: n + 1
end: tick
Host:
    b: tick
end: Host
Host()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
